# Uniform 8192-token capacity revision before candidate quality collection

This version supersedes input-plan digest
`32b9464fb1f332263932db3b4e5a5278ee267a77d100f5ca0d6be4158b589282` solely for
new quality collection. The old frozen directory, execution identity, producer
bytes and native attempt remain intact.

Root observed two `finish_reason=length` outputs among the first 24 finished
cases of `native-quality-hccl-true-01` at the original 2048-token cap. Because
the prespecified gate requires every control and candidate case to finish
without truncation, that native-only attempt cannot qualify. Root is preserving
and terminating that attempt. This is a failed output-capacity design, not a
measured plugin quality failure. No candidate quality outputs had been
collected when root authorized this revision.

`frozen-v2` retains exactly the same 200 cases, gold labels, raw prompts,
thinking-false token IDs, 25 fixed batches, seed-first admission, parser and
acceptance conditions. All source-file hashes are unchanged. No case is
selected, removed or replaced because of its native result. Truncated outputs
remain wrong/incomplete; the scoring rule is not relaxed.

For every arm, uniformly change `max_tokens` from 2048 to 8192. The longest
prompt is2495 tokens, so maximum prompt+output is10687, below max-model-len16384.
The coordinator bound becomes215300 steps and collection bound10800 seconds;
root's outer process bound is11100 seconds. Temperature0, seed42, EOS behavior,
other runtime settings and all acceptance gates remain unchanged.

Both native controls, raw and grouped candidates must run fresh under the new
plan. The first24 old outputs cannot be reused as v2 control data. The unchanged
driver/scorer binds every run to its plan digest and will reject cross-version
mixing. Core/Ascend/plugin identity, exact existing dirty-build identity,
environment matching, per-batch mixed-P/D receipts, stable-native-correct veto,
aggregate floor and confidence limitations remain as documented in
`QUALITY-PLAN.md`.

This is explicitly an output-budget revision informed by a failed native-only
pilot, before candidate outcomes. It is not a claim that the original capacity
choice passed, or that8192 guarantees completion. Further truncations would
still fail this version's unchanged completion gate.
